### PHASE 1 — Basic Authentication
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# TODO: Find the Basic Auth endpoint in api/urls.py.
# TODO: Write a GET request that sends credentials using the
#       Authorization: Basic <base64(username:password)> header.
#       Tip: REST Client supports  Authorization: Basic admin admin123  directly.

### Phase 1 — Synthesis Challenge: Attacker replay
# An attacker who intercepts "Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM=" off an unencrypted
# connection can replay this exact header without ever knowing it decodes to
# admin:admin123. Base64 is reversible encoding, not encryption — the server
# just decodes and string-matches against the DB, so the encoded string IS
# the credential in practice. This is only safe over HTTPS.
### Phase 1 — Basic Auth (authenticated)
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/basic/
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM=


### Phase 1 — Basic Auth (unauthenticated)
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/basic/ HTTP/1.1

###





